WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.161
Chapter five.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:04.085
Obesity is a risk factor for type two diabetes,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.412
but the connection is more than a label.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.860
The supplied notes describe
insulin resistance: cells have difficulty

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.146
using the insulin present.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.280
Watch the tissue response
weaken while insulin remains available.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.260
Contrast this with type
one diabetes, where autoimmune destruction

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.720
reduces the pancreatic beta-cell supply.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.265
Family history also changes risk.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.630
Exercise and weight management
address modifiable contributors; they do

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.771
not erase inherited susceptibility.
